# Implementation Plan: Enhance Modifier Selection UI

**Branch**: `001-enhance-modifier-ui` | **Date**: 2026-04-17 | **Spec**: [spec.md](./spec.md)
**Input**: Feature specification from `/specs/001-enhance-modifier-ui/spec.md`

**Note**: This template is filled in by the `/speckit.plan` command. See `.specify/templates/plan-template.md` for the execution workflow.

## Summary

Enhance the modifier selection UI for the Lethal Company mod with two main features:
1. **Pre-game selection screen**: Accessible via Escape key before run starts, supports multi-select with confirmation summary
2. **In-game overlay**: Press F2 during active gameplay to view currently active modifiers in a non-intrusive overlay

The current UI is a basic single-selection panel. The enhanced UI will provide a polished, intuitive interface with visual design improvements, modifier descriptions, categories, and a read-only in-game overlay.

## Technical Context

**Language/Version**: C# 12 (targeting .NET Standard 2.1)  
**Primary Dependencies**: Lib.Harmony 2.4.2, UnityEngine.UI, Unity TextMeshPro  
**Storage**: In-memory (no persistence required per spec assumption)  
**Testing**: Manual testing required (no automated test framework present)  
**Target Platform**: Windows (Lethal Company game via BepInEx)  
**Project Type**: Game mod / Unity UI application  
**Performance Goals**: UI animations at 60fps, <100ms input responsiveness, overlay opens in <500ms  
**Constraints**: Must work within Unity's UI system, compatibility with BepInEx 5.x, hotkey F2 must not conflict with game controls  
**Scale/Scope**: 4-50 modifiers, pre-game selection UI + in-game overlay (max 20% screen coverage)

